<%- include('partials/head') %>
<div class="wrap narrow">
  <h1>QR scan test</h1>
  <p class="lead">Open this page on a laptop or second screen. Scan each code below with the <strong>wallet's own scanner</strong> and note what happens. The same bank PID request is encoded four ways, so we can tell what the scanner accepts.</p>
  <p class="note">Only have the phone? A wallet cannot scan the screen it runs on, so use the <strong>Open variant … in the wallet app</strong> buttons instead. That tests the same link content without the scanner.</p>
  <ul class="plain">
    <li><strong>The wallet shows the share / consent screen</strong> → this form works.</li>
    <li><strong>"An error happened while trying to process the QR code"</strong> → the wallet read the code but refused its content.</li>
    <li><strong>Nothing happens</strong> → the wallet could not read the code (too dense).</li>
    <li>Any other message (for example "invalid request"): note its text. The content was understood.</li>
  </ul>
  <% variants.forEach(function (v) { %>
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="v-<%= v.key %>">
    <h2 id="v-<%= v.key %>"><%= v.key %> – <%= v.title %></h2>
    <p class="note"><%= v.length %> characters</p>
    <% if (v.qr) { %><img class="qr <%= v.length > 400 ? 'qr-wide' : 'qr-small' %>" src="<%= v.qr %>" width="<%= v.length > 400 ? 720 : 240 %>" height="<%= v.length > 400 ? 720 : 240 %>" alt="QR code for variant <%= v.key %>"><% } %>
    <p><a class="btn btn-small btn-secondary" href="<%= v.link %>">Open variant <%= v.key %> in the wallet app<span class="sr-only"> (tap this on the phone that has the wallet)</span></a></p>
    <details class="raw"><summary>Show link</summary><p><code class="break"><%= v.link %></code></p></details>
  </section>
  <% }) %>
  <p class="note">Technical page for integrators. Each code starts a real (unsigned) verification request that expires after a few minutes.</p>
</div>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
